  "vector_memory": {
    "semantic_summary": "ScreenBlitPass is a specialized render pass responsible for presenting the final rendered output to the main display canvas. It operates by utilizing a fullscreen quad shader to sample a provided sourceTexture and draw it across the entire viewport. Architecturally, it acts as the terminal stage in the rendering pipeline, managing WebGL context interactions to perform the final texture blit operation."
  },
